---
import PublicationLayout from "../layouts/PublicationLayout.astro";
import { repositoryUrl } from "../lib/publication";
---

<PublicationLayout title="Our approach">
    <header class="page-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p>
        <h1>
            Evidence before
            <br />
            <em>excitement.</em>
        </h1>
        <p>A publication for people putting AI to work in materials science.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="article-body">
        <h2>What belongs here</h2>
        <p>
            New methods, meaningful results, useful software, and better data. We cover discovery,
            simulation, characterization, and autonomous experiments with an emphasis on what a
            materials researcher can learn or use.
        </p>
        <h2>Entirely AI-generated</h2>
        <p>
            Material Intelligence is an experiment in a purely AI-generated news outlet. AI selects
            the stories, summarizes the sources, and writes the articles. The reporting and
            commentary are not written by human journalists or independently fact-checked by a
            human. A publication approval step does not change that authorship or guarantee
            accuracy.
        </p>
        <p>
            Our weekly workflow is being prepared. The launch field notes are background reading,
            not current weekly news. People can suggest sources and report errors through GitHub;
            the publication's articles are generated by AI.
        </p>
        <h2>Read the original</h2>
        <p>
            Substantive claims link to primary sources. A preprint is labeled as a preprint, an
            announcement as an announcement, and abstract-only coverage as such. Predicted stability
            is not proof of experimental synthesis. Benchmarks do not establish universal
            performance.
        </p>
        <h2>Community contributions</h2>
        <p>
            Submit a paper, release, or capability through a{" "}
            <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/issues/new?template=story.yml`}>story suggestion</a>, or
            contribute a submission file through a pull request. Tell us what changed, why it
            matters, and whether you are affiliated with the work. Suggestions are assessed for
            evidence and relevance; requested features are not guaranteed placement.
        </p>
        <h2>Corrections and transparency</h2>
        <p>
            AI can misread sources, miss context, and produce incorrect claims or citations. Treat
            this publication as a starting point for reading the original work.{" "}
            <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/issues/new?template=correction.yml`}>Report a correction</a>{" "}
            with the article URL and supporting source. Material corrections receive a dated note in
            the article; changes remain visible in the repository history. We do not currently
            accept paid placements.
        </p>
    </div>
</PublicationLayout>
